# Security

**When:** changing auth, inbound validation, secrets handling, CORS, rate limits, or vuln-sensitive deps.

Never trust user input. Prefer maintained libraries over custom crypto.

---

## Rules

- **Validate and sanitize** all inbound data before use.
- **SQL injection:** parameterized queries only — no exceptions.
- **Authentication:** validate tokens in **middleware**. Never roll your own crypto. Handlers read identity from context.
- **Secrets:** env / secret managers only — never commit secrets. Redact in logs.
- **TLS:** inter-service traffic over TLS; terminate at LB/mesh as appropriate.
- **Rate limiting:** public endpoints — per-IP default; per-user when authenticated.
- **Body size:** `http.MaxBytesReader` on all request bodies.
- **CORS:** allowlist origins — never `*` in production for authenticated APIs.
- **Dependencies:** run `govulncheck`; pin majors; avoid shady transitive history.
- **Least privilege:** app DB roles only what stores need — no superuser from app code.

---

## Do not

- Parse auth inside individual handlers when middleware exists.
- Log tokens, passwords, or raw credentials.
- Disable TLS verification in production paths.
- Accept unbounded request bodies.
